INTRODUCTION

Wine for illumos-based distros.

REQUIREMENTS

To compile and run Wine, you must have one of the following:

  Illumos-based distros (Tested on OpenIndiana)

OpenIndiana info:
  The following dependencies are required: gcc-14, flex, bison, gnu-make, header-audio, nvidia-# (tested on Quadro T600 with nvidia-470)

QUICK START

From the top-level directory of the Wine source (which contains this file),
run:

./patches/configure-wine-8.0.2.sh
gmake
cp ./patches/env.sh.example ${WINE_PREFIX}/bin/env.sh

Then either install Wine:

gmake install

Or run Wine directly from the build directory:

cd ${WINE_PREFIX}/bin
source ./env.sh
./wine notepad

INSTALL SVR4 RELEASE PACKAGE

sudo pkgadd -d <pkgname.pkg>

